{% doc %}
  One product row in the search drawer — thumbnail plus uppercase title.

  Rendered from both branches of sections/isoa-search-drawer.liquid: the idle
  "recommended" list and the predictive results list. The reference uses one
  row design for both states, so the markup lives here rather than being
  written out twice and left to drift.

  The image box is a fixed square that the artwork is fitted into rather than
  cropped to (`object-fit: contain` in rhode-drawers.css) — the reference
  renders its thumbnails the same way, via `background-size: contain` on a
  lazysizes padding box.

  @param {product} product - The product to render.

  @example
  {% render 'isoa-search-drawer-product', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

<a class="isoa-sd__product" href="{{ product.url }}">
  {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
    <span class="isoa-sd__product-image">
      <img
        src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 246 }}"
        alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
        width="123"
        height="123"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      >
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
  <span class="isoa-sd__product-title">{{ product.title }}</span>
</a>
